<html xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" xmlns:w="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Specification</title></head><body><p> <strong>Functional Specification Document - Taschenrechner - Grundrechenarten-Modul</strong></p><p><strong>1. Overview</strong></p><p>This module is designed to implement the fundamental arithmetic operations (Addition, Subtraction, Multiplication, Division). Its purpose is to create a reusable library for internal projects that requires basic arithmetic functionalities.</p><p><strong>2. User Stories</strong></p><ul><li>As a developer, I want to be able to easily integrate the Grundrechenarten-Modul into my project, so that I can save time and effort in implementing basic arithmetic operations.</li><li>As an end-user, I want the module to accurately perform addition, subtraction, multiplication, and division, so that I can rely on the results for my calculations.</li><li>As an end-user, I want the module to prevent division by zero, so that I avoid mathematical errors and inconsistencies in my calculations.</li></ul><p><strong>3. Functional Requirements</strong></p><ol><li>SHALL correctly perform addition, subtraction, multiplication, and division operations.</li><li>SHOULD provide an error message when division by zero occurs.</li><li>MAY support other advanced mathematical functions as future requirements.</li></ol><p><strong>4. User Workflows</strong></p><p>Primary use case: Performing arithmetic operations</p><ol><li>The user calls the appropriate arithmetic function (e.g., add, subtract, multiply, or divide) of the Grundrechenarten-Modul.</li><li>The module performs the specified arithmetic operation using the provided input values.</li><li>The module returns the result of the operation.</li></ol><p><strong>5. UI/UX Considerations</strong></p><ul><li>The module should have a user-friendly API for easy integration.</li><li>The error message for division by zero should be clear and concise.</li></ul><p><strong>6. Data Requirements</strong></p><ul><li>Input data: Two numbers for addition, subtraction, multiplication, and division operations.</li><li>Output data: The result of the performed arithmetic operation.</li><li>The module should support decimal values and handle large numbers as needed.</li></ul><p><strong>7. Integration Points</strong></p><p>The Grundrechenarten-Modul is intended to be integrated into various internal projects. No external APIs or services are required at this time.</p><p><strong>8. Constraints and Assumptions</strong></p><ul><li>The module assumes that the input data is always a valid numerical value (integer or decimal).</li><li>The module does not handle complex numbers or scientific calculations.</li></ul><p><strong>9. Open Questions</strong></p><ul><li>Should the module support advanced mathematical functions like square root or logarithm?</li><li>Should the module provide unit testing examples for developers to easily test the integration?</li></ul><p>This functional specification document aims to provide a clear understanding of the Grundrechenarten-Modul's purpose, requirements, and intended usage. All requirements are testable, measurable, and traceable.</p></body></html>